From 6d449cccb367476701872e683021be769c1f5dca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: linux-a9 <linux-a9@localhost>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 00:15:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: apple-h9p: defer late j71t ports while ANS is missing

The tri46 same-entry warm-boot rescue trace shows Wi-Fi 14e4:43dc
enumerating at 0000:01:00.0 after ANS port 0 failed link training.
The DT maps bus 1 to ANS DART0 at 601008000, so its all-ones
attach/reinit and iommu_setup_default_domain warning are a secondary
wrong-DART attachment, not proof of a shared PMGR power failure.

Programming rescue-bus secondary=2 does not prevent this: the common
ECAM host helper sets PCI_REASSIGN_ALL_BUS before scanning.

Keep late ports unpublished on j71t trial ANS boots until port 0 is
enabled. After a successful explicit ANS rescue and rescan has reserved
bus 1, reschedule late-port work so Wi-Fi can enumerate on bus 2.
Leave the normal ANS-present, Round 7 and other-board paths unchanged.

This guards DART routing. It does not repair the earlier port-0 link
failure and does not add a shared-domain reset or automatic retry.

Validated: actual late-work/rescue functions with ASan/UBSan fixtures
(red on tri46), 23 existing ANS handoff tests, ARM64 object compilation,
and strict checkpatch. No device access or hardware validation.
---
 drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple-h9p.c | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple-h9p.c b/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple-h9p.c
index f3e3f5724e..3a60a3ac3c 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple-h9p.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple-h9p.c
@@ -2796,6 +2796,20 @@ static void apple_h9p_late_ports_work(struct work_struct *work)
 	unsigned int port;
 	int ret;
 
+	/* The DT maps bus 1 to ANS/DART0, bus 2 to Wi-Fi/DART1. The
+	 * generic host scan reassigns buses, overriding rescue_bus(). With
+	 * port 0 absent it gives Wi-Fi bus 1 and attaches it to the stopped
+	 * ANS DART. Leave late ports unpublished until ANS owns bus 1.
+	 */
+	if (of_machine_is_compatible("apple,j71t") &&
+	    pcie->ans_mode != APPLE_ANS_ROUND7 &&
+	    !(READ_ONCE(pcie->enabled_ports) & BIT(0))) {
+		dev_warn(pcie->dev,
+			 "ANS port 0 missing; deferring late ports %#lx to preserve DART routing\n",
+			 pending);
+		return;
+	}
+
 	for_each_set_bit(port, &pending, H9P_NUM_PORTS) {
 		ret = apple_h9p_late_port(pcie, port);
 		if (ret == -EPROBE_DEFER) {
@@ -3085,6 +3099,9 @@ static ssize_t ans_recover_store(struct device *dev,
 out:
 	pcie->ans_rescue_result = ret;
 	pci_unlock_rescan_remove();
+	/* Successful ANS publication reserves bus 1 before Wi-Fi can scan. */
+	if (!ret && pcie->late_ports)
+		schedule_delayed_work(&pcie->late_work, 0);
 	return ret ? ret : count;
 }
 
